  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Africa Clean Energy - Makhado South Africa bioenergy training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norad supports New Africa Clean Energy with training of technical staff for the operation and maintenance of itsTimbadola bioenergy combined heat and power plant, is positioned to be the first biomass-based CHP built within the solid wood products industry of Southern Africa. The plant will burn waste products from local forestry and supply electricity into the grid, as well as heating to the local processing. In addition to allowing NACE to us local staff to operate the plant, training engineers in the plant&apos;s construction and maintenance may allow them to more heavily rely on local expertise when scaling up several more plants in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
